# Ignore python temporary files
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Ignore environmental variables (Secrets)
.env
.env.local
.venv
env/
venv/

# Ignore system files
.DS_Store

# Visual Studio local cache (locked by IDE, never commit)
.vs/

# .NET build output for the two MAUI apps (GustoPOS, GustoWaiter).
#
# Pure build products — every file here is regenerated by `dotnet build`, and
# they are large and binary (DLLs, PDBs, .exe, WinRT .winmd). 16,631 of them
# were committed before this rule existed, which is most of the repo by file
# count and makes any `git status` unreadable.
#
# NOTE: this rule only stops FUTURE ones being added. .gitignore has no effect
# on paths git already tracks, so removing the existing 16,631 from the index
# is a separate change.
gusto_pos/**/bin/
gusto_pos/**/obj/

# Python packaging output for mcp_server.
#
# `pip install .` makes setuptools copy the package into build/lib/ and write
# carevo_mcp.egg-info/ beside the source. Both are regenerated on every build
# and neither was ever committed — unlike the .NET case above, this rule is
# purely preventative, so there is no index to clean up.
#
# Worth having anyway: build/lib/ holds a FROZEN copy of every module, and a
# stale one already caused a wrong answer during a grep for callers of
# /api/v1/public/* — the same file appearing twice, one of them out of date.
mcp_server/build/
mcp_server/*.egg-info/

# Claude Code worktrees (ephemeral, not part of source)
.claude/worktrees/
# --- Credentials and machine-local config --------------------------------
# Added after a security audit found live secrets committed to this PUBLIC
# repository. These rules stop FUTURE additions; they do not remove what git
# already tracks, and they do not rewrite history. Anything that was pushed
# must still be treated as compromised and rotated.

# Claude Code local settings. Machine-specific, and the repo-root copy carried
# the live production Neon DSN — user, host and password — in five places.
.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# Firebase / Google service configs.
#
# SUFFIX-TOLERANT ON PURPOSE. customer_app/android/.gitignore already listed
# `/app/google-services.json` by exact name, and a copy saved as
# `google-services.json.json` sailed straight past it carrying a live Android
# API key (AIzaSy...) for project carevo-5d24c. An exact-name rule only ever
# catches the spelling you thought of.
google-services.json*
**/google-services.json*
GoogleService-Info.plist
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
serviceAccount*.json
**/serviceAccount*.json

# Android signing material.
key.properties
**/key.properties

# .NET app settings for GustoPOS / GustoWaiter — nothing tracked today, so this
# is purely pre-emptive.
**/appsettings.json
**/appsettings.*.json

# Env files as a GLOB, not the two exact names that were here before. .env.prod,
# .env.staging and friends were all tracked-eligible until now.
.env.*
**/.env.*
# ...but the committed placeholder templates are the point of being in git, so
# re-admit them explicitly. These contain no real values.
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
!.env.local.example
!**/.env.local.example
